(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2608180100-runners-do-not-unlock-gates")
  (:adr/title "Adding 256 ClojureScript runners unlocked one JVM gate; what blocks the other 85 is .clj tests and cross-repo deps")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-08-18")
  (:source/dataset "adr")
  (:adr/supersedes "")
  (:adr/superseded-by "")
  (:adr/context
  "ADR-2608170500 landed 437 repositories into the ClojureScript test tier. After
syncing the 390 affected checkouts, `verify-cljs-runner-completeness` sees the work
for the first time: repos with a ClojureScript runner went 201 -> 457, complete ones
181 -> 438, and the population with portable tests and no runner 2,034 -> 1,778. The
real share of portable suites any ClojureScript host runs went from about 9% to
about 20%.

The implicit expectation was that this would let a corresponding number of fleet
gates move off `:jvm-test`. It did not, and the reason is worth writing down before
anyone repeats the tranche expecting a different result.")

  (:adr/decision
  "Measure which `:jvm-test` gates can actually move, against all four admission
  conditions in `scripts/fleet-ci/gates.edn`, rather than against condition 4 alone.
  Move the ones that pass. Record the ceiling.")

  (:adr/body
  "## The measurement (2026-08-18)

86 `:jvm-test` gates. 18 of them target a repository that now has a COMPLETE
ClojureScript runner — condition 4 satisfied. Of those 18:

| | n | why it still cannot move |
|---|---|---|
| condition 3 | **14** | the test path needs a sibling repo, and `:nbb-test`'s classpath is the shipped tree only |
| condition 1 | **3** | the repo also has `.clj` tests, so the JVM count is higher |
| **passes all four** | **1** | `ongaku` |

Condition 1's three, with the numbers that expose them:

    org-ietf-deflate   JVM 34 tests / 488 assertions   nbb 23 / 202   (.clj tests: 2)
    org-ietf-zstd      JVM 28 / 251                    nbb 20 / 173   (.clj tests: 1)
    proto              (no :test output)               nbb 11 /  79   (.clj tests: 1)

## The thing to take away

**A complete ClojureScript runner is not a licence to flip the gate.**

`verify-cljs-runner-completeness` measures whether every PORTABLE deftest namespace
is run. That is the right question for the runner and it is correctly answered:
`org-ietf-deflate`'s runner covers all of its portable tests. But the repo also
holds two `.clj` test namespaces, which no ClojureScript host can run, and which
`clojure -M:test` does run. Moving that gate to `:nbb-test` would leave those two
namespaces run by nobody, while the receipt still said `Ran N tests`.

Condition 1 — identical `Ran N tests containing M assertions` under both runtimes —
is what catches this, and it is why the admission list has four conditions rather
than one. This ADR exists because the obvious shortcut (\"the gate says complete, so
flip it\") was the shortcut taken to build the candidate list, and condition 1
rejected three of the four survivors.

## What this implies for the JVM exit

The two blockers scale differently:

- **cross-repo deps (14)** are a property of `:nbb-test`'s design, not of the
  repositories. They do not go away by writing more runners. Either the gate kind
  learns to ship a classpath, or those repos stay on the JVM.
- **`.clj` tests (3 here, 1,657 repos workspace-wide)** go away only by porting the
  tests, which is the `:jvm-source` debt ADR-2608170200 counts at 954 repos.

So the route to fewer `:jvm-test` gates is not more ClojureScript runners. Adding
256 of them moved exactly one gate. It is porting `.clj` — and that is the same
work item that is still at 954, untouched.

The tranche was still worth landing: 3,412 tests / 34,612 assertions now run on a
runtime where a cljs-half defect in a `.cljc` is visible, and 14 repositories were
found to fail there while green on the JVM. That is the value. Unlocking gates was
not.")

  (:adr/consequences
  "- `ongaku` moves to `:nbb-test`: `.clj` tests 0, both runtimes 30 tests / 111
  assertions, self-contained, and it exits 1 with `territory-covers?`'s `every?`
  changed to `some` and 0 with it intact.
- `gates.edn` records why the other 17 did not move, next to the entry, so the
  candidate list is not rebuilt from condition 4 alone.
- Anyone proposing 'write runners to get off the JVM' now has the measured
  conversion rate: 256 runners -> 1 gate.
- The `:nbb-test` gate kind could be given a classpath, which would unblock the 14.
  That is a change to `tick.cljs` and is not made here.")

  (:adr/evidence
  (vector "scripts/fleet-ci/gates.edn"
   "verify-cljs-runner-completeness after west update: 457 with-runner, 438 complete, 1778 without"
   "verify-jvm-dependency-surface after west update: bb.edn 363 -> 186, jvm-source 954 unchanged"))
  (:adr/related
  (vector "adr-2608170500-two-tranches-landed-437-repos"
   "adr-2608170300-cljs-runner-completeness-gate"
   "adr-2608170200-jvm-dependency-surface-measured-repowide"))))
